Offline by default. Network access to pypi.org occurs only when the user explicitly approves --online.\"\nmetadata:\n  author: \"Matt Van Horn\"\n  version: \"1.0.0\"\n  source: \"https://github.com/Shubhamsaboo/awesome-llm-apps\"", "declared_name": "dependency-doctor", "format_status": "header_present_not_schema_validated"}
{"id": "2e7f5abe45a897751acd", "repository": "Shubhamsaboo/awesome-llm-apps", "commit_sha": "c129f31036f5ba0bba42cbb63937a66946fdf2c0", "skill_path": "agent_skills/first-reader/SKILL.md", "source_url": "https://github.com/Shubhamsaboo/awesome-llm-apps/blob/c129f31036f5ba0bba42cbb63937a66946fdf2c0/agent_skills/first-reader/SKILL.md", "git_blob_sha": "c1b70637ad31cf712556241fc97e0a172dd3cf44", "sha256": "a0947f733e838b8a29d6860d9077356bfac5edd9be13c75a12d974ae501f298f", "bytes": 17170, "collected_at": "2026-11-06T12:10:30.507191+00:00", "state": "collected", "raw_path": "raw/Shubhamsaboo/awesome-llm-apps/c129f31036f5ba0bba42cbb63937a66946fdf2c0/agent_skills/first-reader/SKILL.md", "execution_status": "not_executed", "quality_status": "not_evaluated", "license_candidates": ["LICENSE"], "repository_manifest": "manifests/Shubhamsaboo/awesome-llm-apps/c129f31036f5ba0bba42cbb63937a66946fdf2c0.json", "local_package_files": ["agent_skills/first-reader/README.md", "agent_skills/first-reader/SKILL.md", "agent_skills/first-reader/references/interview.md", "agent_skills/first-reader/references/personas.md", "agent_skills/first-reader/references/report.md", "agent_skills/first-reader/references/room.md", "agent_skills/first-reader/scripts/ask.py", "agent_skills/first-reader/scripts/feed.py", "agent_skills/first-reader/scripts/recall.py", "agent_skills/first-reader/scripts/room.py", "agent_skills/first-reader/scripts/room_template.html", "agent_skills/first-reader/scripts/signals.py", "agent_skills/first-reader/scripts/skim.py"], "local_package_files_not_exported": [], "external_dependency_status": "not_fetched_or_verified", "path_review_hints": [], "frontmatter_raw": "name: first-reader\ndescription: Beta readers for any draft, run by simulating how a real reader experiences it, moment by moment. A skim gate, a no-lookahead timed read producing an attention transcript with quit points, a recall test of what a reader remembers the next day, and a trust ledger of the implied author. Use when the user asks for a beta read, beta readers, test readers, human review, reader review, to read something like a human, to be a first reader, whether a piece holds attention or will actually get read, for a quick read of whether a busy skimmer would even open a post, what readers will remember or take away tomorrow, where readers stop reading or bounce, or why a draft still feels off or hollow after anti-slop or humanizer edits. Final gate before publishing; reports where the reading broke; never rewrites.\ncompatibility: Python 3 stdlib only, offline, no dependencies. feed.py runs a loopback http server on 127.0.0.1 during a read so reader subagents receive the draft one passage at a time; nothing leaves the machine and there is no external network access.", "declared_name": "first-reader", "format_status": "header_present_not_schema_validated"}
